  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "WEEKNUM with an invalid return_type can answer differently each time it is called",
  "statement": "The documentation says an out-of-range return_type gives #NUM!. Excel usually does, but not always, and the same call can give different answers. In recorded captures of build 20430, 479 (serial_number, return_type) pairs were read with different results: usually #NUM!, sometimes a number (0, 1, 9, 10, 53 or 54), and some pairs differ within one run file. In build 20527 a matrix of 1,926 pairs (serial_number 0, 1, 59, 60, 61 and 43831, return_type -32 to 288) was read twice in one request, and 623 pairs differed between the two readings: 619 between a number and #NUM!, and 4 between 9 and 10. Every difference has an undocumented return_type. The ten documented return_types (1, 2, 11 to 17 and 21) gave the same answer both times. No rule for the undocumented values is claimed.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "The readings conflict with each other. The 479 comes from the DnaCalc witness differences file. The 1,926 pairs come from one request of 3,852 calls, with exact input read-backs, compared pair by pair.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": {
    "claim": "If Return_type is out of the range specified in the table above, a #NUM! error is returned.",
    "source": "https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/weeknum-function-e5c43a03-b4ab-426c-b411-b18c13c75340"
  },
